  Version 0.1.39 (2026-11-06)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * debsums is a Depends (ORDER 437). --debsums is a feature of the package,
    and "a dependency a designed feature needs is a Depends" (Daniel,
    2026-11-02, memory design-check-every-default); 0.1.38 had it as a
    Suggests. debsums is 108 KB installed (Depends libdpkg-perl,
    libfile-fnmatch-perl, perl). --debsums still says what to do when debsums
    was removed afterwards (LOCAL81, exit 2).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.38 (2026-11-06)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * --debsums [PACKAGE...]: Lean Code's front for debsums (ORDER 252c, J16).
    debsums checks every file against its package's md5sums, and a projected
    file is not its package's bytes by design, so debsums alone calls every
    lean file changed. The front checks the projected files by their lean
    hashes (what --verify does) and sends every other file to debsums; a file
    debsums names that dpkg-stereo projected is not counted twice. A file
    debsums finds changed or missing is printed as DEBSUMS and is a problem
    (exit 1). A package without an md5sums file is information (NOSUMS, not
    counted). debsums not installed, not finishing or asked for an unknown
    package is an incomplete check, said with what to do, exit 2, never clean.
    debsums itself is a Suggests, and a row of the developer task.
    Messages LOCAL81 to LOCAL85 in the nine languages. Test:
    test/debsums-front-test.sh (control: debsums alone calls the projected
    files changed; green; four reds).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.37 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * --verify --deep exits 0 on a healthy, just-upgraded system (ORDER 398).
    A check that is red on a healthy system proves nothing (the proof of
    release r1103a: dist-upgrade exit 0, --verify 0 problems, --deep 27).
  * A file that is not a conffile, whose installed bytes today's renderer does
    not reproduce, but which passes restore's own checks (the owner lists the
    path and is at the recorded version, the owner's md5sums, the original's
    md5 and sha256, the installed bytes against the recorded projection), is
    printed as OLDFORM, information, and not counted: an earlier renderer's
    form, which restore takes back from its original. Any other mismatch
    stays MISMATCH and counted, a conffile always needs the exact render.
  * --deep also compares the lc1 manifest rows dpkg-stereo did not project
    with their build-time payload, to know the package's own files are
    intact. One that differs is printed as AFTERINST, information, and not
    counted: depmod rewrites modules.dep at every kernel install, and
    maintainer scripts rewrite os-release, issue and plymouthd.defaults;
    dpkg-stereo did not project them and leaves them. A projected row that
    differs, or a row that is gone, stays LCCHANGED and counted.
  * The summary line names both information counts, and the exit status
    follows the problems only (0, 1 for a problem, 2 for an incomplete check).
    Messages LOCAL77 to LOCAL80 in the nine languages.

