  Version 0.1.32 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * A configure with no pending conffile needs no native-capability subprocess;
    use the existing package snapshot to return before querying dpkg.
  * Carry 0.1.31's orphan recovery and removed-conffile restoration. The older-dpkg
    pre-invoke path and explicit restore also require exact reproduction from the
    original independently identified by the owning package before writing; a
    refusal keeps the file and names its reason through the problems engine.
  * With native dpkg conffile capability 2, pre-invoke restores no conffile.
    Both the running binary's hook signal and its package's Provides must
    advertise the capability; older dpkg retains the restore path.
  * Keep native conffile refusals in the problems engine, naming the package,
    file, reason and remaining .dpkg-dist/.dpkg-new. Repair only rechecks.
    Messages ship in all nine edition languages.
  * Retain conffile records across separate unpack/configure runs, and remove
    them if the unpacked package is purged before configuration.
  * Share the exact original-to-projection byte comparison between --verify
    and /usr/lib/dpkg-stereo/conffile-verify, the read-only verifier for the
    edition's dpkg. Select the reader from the original and installed path.
  * Recheck original MD5/SHA-256 and current SHA-256 at the verifier boundary;
    reject forged lean hashes even when the pristine original is genuine.
  * Isolate Python imports, require a protected root-owned renderer, and
    refuse writes and external processes during verification.

